          "after": [
            "**When to use שֶׁל and when the construct form?** A practical rule: if the link is **someone's ownership**, use שֶׁל — הַסֵּפֶר שֶׁל דָּנָה. If the link is a **type or category** — a school *of the book kind*, a card *of the credit kind* — use the construct form. The construct makes one new term; שֶׁל only shows the owner.",
            "⚠️ **You can't put an adjective in the middle of a construct.** \"A new credit card\" is כַּרְטִיס אַשְׁרַאי חָדָשׁ — the adjective goes at the end, after both nouns."
          ]
