          "text": "⚠️ **אוֹפַנַּיִם** (bicycle) ends in ־ַיִם, the pair form — two wheels. Just like מִשְׁקָפַיִם and נַעֲלַיִם. Hebrew consistently sees two-wheeled things as a pair, much as English says *bi*-cycle."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "**Israeli public transport stops completely during Shabbat** — from Friday afternoon to Saturday evening, in almost the whole country. The only things running are the **מוֹנִית שֵׁרוּת** *(monit sherut)*, minibus shared taxis on fixed routes, and regular taxis. This is a practical matter, not a cultural footnote: plan a Saturday trip without knowing it and you'll be stuck."
